From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: r-ccu: source 000 is the DCXO, not SYS_CLK24M

The R-CCU's three bus clocks all take their source index 000 from the device
tree's "hosc", which is osc24M. The A733 UM gives index 000 as DCXO for all
three: AHBS_CLK_SRC_SEL "000: DCXO" (V0.92 4.2.5.1), APBS0_CLK_SRC_SEL and
APBS1_CLK_SRC_SEL the same (4.2.5.2, 4.2.5.3). On this SoC the DCXO is the
26 MHz crystal; SYS_CLK24M is what REF_PLL makes out of it, and the two are a
different net. `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-feed-pll-ref-from-the-dcxo` fixed exactly this confusion on the main CCU and said in
its header that the R-CCU half was out of scope; this is that half.

It is a live misrate, not a cosmetic one. Under our boot chain APBS0 sits on
index 000 (APBS0_CLK = 0x00000000, M = 0), so r-apb0 is fed 26 MHz while the
driver reports 24 MHz -- 8 % low. Its only consumer today is r_pio's "apb"
clock, which enables it and never reads its rate, but a rate that is wrong is
wrong before anyone reads it.

Measured on silicon rather than argued from the manual. APBS1 is the one bus
clock in this block with a consumer whose rate is observable from outside --
the PMIC I2C hangs off it -- so its source field was moved from 100 to 000 and
back, with FACTOR_M left at 0 and the TWI divider untouched at 3200, and the
same transfer timed in each state (128-byte against 8-byte read, differenced,
so per-transfer overhead cancels):

    source 100   1211 us/byte      predicted at 24 MHz: 1200 us
    source 000   1116 us/byte      predicted at 26 MHz: 1107 us
    source 100   1218 us/byte      (restored; the change tracks the source,
                                    not drift)

1214.5 / 1116 = 1.088 against 26 / 24 = 1.083. Index 000 is the 26 MHz DCXO
and index 100 is the 24 MHz net, both as the manual says and neither as the
driver modelled it.

So point index 000 at a "dcxo" input in both parent tables. The device tree
side -- giving the r_ccu node that input -- is `arm64-dts-a733-r-ccu-dcxo-input`: the node is added by `arm64-dts-a733-aon-pinctrl-usb-host-vbus`,
which applies long after this one, so the two halves cannot ride in one patch.
Neither half does anything without the other, and `arm64-dts-a733-r-ccu-dcxo-input` says so too.

Falsifier (needs both halves): clk_summary must report r-apb0 at 26000000 with
APBS0_CLK still 0x00000000, and r-apb1 must stay at 24000000 (it sits on index
100, which `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-r-ccu-apbs-source-100-is-sys-clk24m` already corrected and which this patch does not touch).

Assisted-by: Claude

--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60iw2-r.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60iw2-r.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
 #include "ccu-sun60iw2-r.h"
 
 static const struct clk_parent_data r_ahb_parents[] = {
-	{ .fw_name = "hosc" },			/* 000: DCXO 24M */
+	{ .fw_name = "dcxo" },			/* 000: DCXO, 26 MHz */
 	{ .fw_name = "losc" },			/* 001: RTC 32k */
 	{ .fw_name = "iosc" },			/* 010: RC 16M */
 	{ .fw_name = "pll-periph-200m" },	/* 011: PERIPLL-200M */
@@ -48,7 +48,7 @@
  * 7.3 kHz on the wire against the 100 kHz the device tree asks for.
  */
 static const struct clk_parent_data r_apbs_parents[] = {
-	{ .fw_name = "hosc" },			/* 000: DCXO 24M */
+	{ .fw_name = "dcxo" },			/* 000: DCXO, 26 MHz */
 	{ .fw_name = "losc" },			/* 001: RTC 32k */
 	{ .fw_name = "iosc" },			/* 010: RC 16M */
 	{ .fw_name = "pll-periph-200m" },	/* 011: PERIPLL-200M */
